description:
FILED s543h (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-22), found by member 1's (#2630) breaking-shape probe.  PRE-EXISTING: base 5e8b88c0 and the s543h tree answer the same.

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 | ./runpcl):
    my $x = "lex";
    package Foo;
    sub g { $x }
    package main;
    $main::x = "pkg";
    print "1 ", Foo::g(), " $main::x\n";        # 1 lex pkg   | 1 pkg pkg
    $main::y = "glob";
    print "2 ", eval(q{$y}), "\n";               # 2 glob      | 2 (empty)
    my $y = "lexy";
    package Bar;
    sub h { $y }
    package main;
    print "3 ", Bar::h(), " ", eval(q{$y}), "\n";   # = perl (control)

WHAT IT IS: a file lexical used in a LATER package section is SPAN-promoted (`$x__file__N`, Parser2::_rename_spanning_lexicals); in a file with a string eval it still takes the M-F alias (`p-alias-eval-cell '$x CELL`), which writes the lexical's box into the package variable of its name -- so the qualified write `$main::x = "pkg"` writes the LEXICAL (row 1).  And its eval pair is published SEGMENT-wide (_publish_span_pair), so an eval BEFORE the declaration names the cell (row 2: perl reads $main::y).

FIX DIRECTION (designed, not taken -- s543h's mechanism): s543h publishes a CAPTURE-promoted segment cell per eval WORD (Parser2::_publish_eval_cell: the binder says which words' pads see the declaration, the cell qualified from another package) and drops the program unit's alias for it (_eval_reach_promoted).  The span pass is the other promoter: call _publish_eval_cell for its cells (the binding is the span record's `b`) instead of _publish_span_pair, and skip the alias in the program unit (_eval_reach_promoted's published branch, _emb_promoted_cells).  BAR: the reproducer + rows with the eval in a later section, in a sub defined above the decl, a nested eval, a dynamic eval; the wide A/B (every span-promoted cell in a file with an eval moves: the pair's spelling and its positions); the sweep (name resolution).

Not s543h's: its members are the capture route (#2630), `our` aliases (#2557), the free-name parameters (#2091), state cells (#4821).


=== DONE (s543k) === (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-22/23; WIP 2)
The span pass's cells take the route s543h built for capture-promoted ones: Parser2::_publish_span_cell -> _publish_eval_words (the per-word half of _publish_eval_cell: the binder's answer at each string-eval word) + _eval_cell_published, so the PROGRAM unit takes no M-F alias (_eval_reach_promoted's published branch; an embedded span declarator through _emb_promoted_cells -> _eval_reach_promoted); the segment map is read only by a word-less site (eval_site_span_cells).  `$main::x = ...` no longer writes the lexical; an eval before the declaration / in a sub above it reads the package variable.
Probes (scratch/s543k/p2/probes.txt, 21 shapes incl. a module by require and by use, BEGIN, two lexicals in two sections, symbolic ${"main::x"}, our re-declared, local $main::x, nested / dynamic / interpolation / s///ee sites): base = perl 3, tree = perl 18; PCL_OPT=none prints identically.  Left: an IDENTITY cell seen by an eval in a sub above the declaration (#5352, the capture route does the same); a module (non-program unit keeps the alias, #2640).  Guard eval-capture-01.t span_before span_qual span_eval (fail on 4a0fd0ec) + span_early (control).
